> On Sunday 11 April 2010 07:08:57 Kevin Reid wrote:
>>   zirpu skari be lo tunka ku tsani
>
> I'd say "zirpu tukska tsani".

Ah, I like.

An intermediate (not defining any lujvo) version would be

   zirpu ke tunka skari ke'e tsani

"ke...ke'e" are parentheses for tanru:

   (purple (copper color)) sky

whereas the default left-grouped "zirpu tunka skari tsani" is

   ((purple copper) color) sky

